continue-waiting-through-model-safety-buffering

Lane: frontend

FlatPatch: continue-waiting-through-model-safety-buffering

Form: GitDiff

Segment: snapshot

Purpose: Continue the active request through model safety buffering without presenting a faster-model retry menu or requiring user action.

Requires: none

Provides: Show the waiting status once for the active live turn, leave the composer and unrelated menus usable, ignore historical or stale updates, and restore ordinary status when output begins, buffering clears or the turn ends. Disable native menu activation and its exclusive submitted-turn collection while preserving the upstream confirmation event, menu implementation and tests.

Boundary: Do not change the selected model, submit or interrupt from buffering notifications, or alter server safety policy. Preserve native explicit retry execution and its permission, fork, draft and goal-continuation semantics, as well as native reasoning status restoration and input recovery.

Verification: Focused live waiting tests cover repeated notifications, composer input, side conversations, lifecycle reset, response start, replay filtering and modal preservation; retained native menu and explicit retry integration tests cover confirmation, first-turn and repeated retry, settings, drafts and permissions.


